      A('PCK-CHEM-FORMULA-ANATOMY','FORMULA_ANATOMY_AND_CHARGE',['CAP-READ-FORMULA','CAP-PARSE-ION-CHARGE'],'Treat the formula as a structured message, not a string of characters.',['Point separately to symbol, subscript, coefficient and charge positions.','Map each position to its local meaning.'],'Read position first, then meaning: a lower numeral, a leading numeral and an upper charge do different jobs.','Do not infer chemical facts beyond the notation and source-authorized rules.',['Locate notation features.','Name each feature.','State its local meaning.','Check the whole species identity.'],'Move one numeral between coefficient, subscript and charge positions while keeping the symbols fixed.','PF-FORMULA_CHARGE_PARSE','All nearby numerals mean the same thing.','Ask what changes chemically when the numeral moves to another position.',['Re-anchor to position.','Name the notation feature.','Retry on a new source-authorized formula.'],['Check symbol identity.','Check subscript/charge position.'],['remove position labels','combine two notation features'],'formula/charge discrimination in a new species',['Does not supply oxidation states, valencies or charges not authorized upstream.']),
      A('PCK-CHEM-NOTATION-DISCRIMINATION','SUBSCRIPT_COEFFICIENT_CHARGE_DISCRIMINATION',['CAP-READ-FORMULA','CAP-PARSE-ION-CHARGE'],'Use a side-by-side notation pair rather than a warning alone.',['Hold element symbols fixed.','Change one numeral position only.'],'The position of the numeral is evidence for what it means.','Read coefficient, subscript and charge as different notation roles.',['Present a minimal pair.','Identify the only changed feature.','Explain the changed meaning.','Retry without labels.'],'Same symbols; one numeral changes only its notation position.','PF-FORMULA_CHARGE_PARSE','The numeral itself carries a fixed meaning wherever it appears.','Ask which chemical quantity or identity is altered by moving that numeral.',['Circle the position.','Name the feature.','Restate the chemical meaning.'],['Check notation position.','Check species identity.'],['remove highlighting','increase visual similarity'],'notation-position discrimination under reduced cues',['Use only notation forms authorized in current scope.']),
      A('PCK-CHEM-CONSERVATION','CONSERVATION_ATOM_CHARGE_SPECIES',['CAP-CHECK-ATOM-CONSERVATION','CAP-VERIFY-CHEMICAL-REPRESENTATION'],'Frame conservation as an accounting check on a represented process.',['Create before/after ledgers for the required invariant.','Keep atom count, charge and species identity as separate ledgers.'],'Count the exact thing the route says must be conserved; different ledgers answer different questions.','The active conservation ledger comes from source/problem-family authority.',['Name the ledger.','Count before/after.','Compare.','Locate the first mismatch.','Recheck after repair.'],'Contrast an atom-count mismatch with a charge or species-identity issue.','PF-CONSERVATION_LEDGER','A balanced-looking expression has passed every chemical check.','Ask which exact invariant was checked and which was not.',['Separate the ledgers.','Repair the failed ledger only.','Run the remaining required checks.'],['Check the required ledger.','Check species identity when applicable.'],['remove ledger headings','combine multiple checks'],'new process with the same conservation obligation',['Does not authorize balancing methods or quantitative invariants outside scope.']),
      A('PCK-CHEM-RULE-EXCEPTION','RULE_PRIORITY_AND_EXCEPTION',['CAP-CHECK-RULE-EXCEPTION','CAP-PRESERVE-REACTION-CONDITION'],'Show the default rule and the gate that can block or modify it.',['Rule cue first.','Condition/exception gate second.','Decision only after the gate check.'],'A remembered rule is incomplete until the stated condition or exception is checked.','Only upstream-recorded rules, conditions and exceptions may populate the gate.',['Select the rule.','Read the condition/exception.','Test applicability.','Apply or withhold the rule.','Verify the condition remains attached.'],'Two cases use the same rule but differ only in the decisive condition/exception.','PF-RULE_WITH_EXCEPTION','Remembering the default rule is enough.','Ask what single feature would make the default rule invalid in this case.',['Re-run the gate.','Name the decisive condition.','Retry on a close contrast.'],['Check conditions.','Check exception status.'],['hide the gate label','embed the condition in notation or prose'],'same rule with a less obvious condition/exception',['Does not create new exceptions; absent conditions stay absent.']),
      A('PCK-CHEM-OBSERVATION-CLAIM','OBSERVATION_EVIDENCE_CLAIM',['CAP-SEPARATE-OBSERVATION-INFERENCE'],'Start with what was actually observed before naming a chemical conclusion.',['Record observation.','State claim separately.','Use an explicit evidence-to-claim link.'],'An observation is evidence; a claim must not say more than that evidence supports.','Source observations and authorized conclusions constrain the reasoning chain.',['Record the observation literally.','State a candidate claim.','Explain the link.','Test for overclaim.'],'Pair the same observation with one supported claim and one overstrong claim.','PF-EVIDENCE_TO_CLAIM','A chemically plausible claim is automatically supported.','Ask which words in the observation support each part of the claim.',['Trim unsupported claim content.','Restate the evidence link.','Retry on another observation.'],['Check observation fidelity.','Check claim strength.'],['remove column labels','add a plausible distractor claim'],'new observation requiring cautious inference',['Does not infer substances or mechanisms not authorized by source.']),
      A('PCK-CHEM-CHANGE-CLASSIFICATION','REACTION_PROCESS_CLASSIFICATION',['CAP-CLASSIFY-CHANGE-EVIDENCE'],'Anchor classification in the supplied evidence or process description.',['Evidence features lead to a criterion; the criterion leads to the class.'],'Name the evidence before naming the class.','Classification criteria must come from source/canonical authority in declared scope.',['Extract evidence.','Select the criterion.','Compare.','Classify.','Verify that the evidence supports the label.'],'Use two cases with similar wording but different decisive evidence.','PF-REACTION_OR_PROCESS_CLASSIFICATION','A familiar word in the prompt is enough to classify the process.','Ask which observation or representation feature actually decides the class.',['Return to the evidence.','Apply the criterion explicitly.','Retry on the near contrast.'],['Check criterion.','Check evidence-to-class link.'],['remove criterion cue','add irrelevant surface detail'],'near-neighbour classification with new evidence',['Does not add reaction categories outside scope.']),
      A('PCK-CHEM-SPECIES-ROLE','SPECIES_ROLE_AND_SPECTATOR',['CAP-TRACK-REACTING-SPECIES','CAP-ATTACH-SPECIES-ROLE'],'Treat the equation as a before/after map of the same chemical entities.',['Track changing species first.','Separate unchanged or spectator information.','Attach a role only after the change is established.'],'A role is proved from what a species does in this equation, not from reagent reputation.','Equation/source evidence is authoritative; memorized reagent reputation is not.',['Identify reactant species.','Track each through the equation.','Mark change/no change.','Attach the role to the reactant evidence.','Verify spectators are not mislabelled.'],'Compare a changed species with an unchanged/spectator species in the same representation.','PF-AGENT_ROLE_ASSIGNMENT','A familiar reagent has one permanent role.','Hide the reagent name and ask whether its role can still be proved from the equation.',['Return to species tracking.','Name the self-change before the role.','Retry with a new equation/representation.'],['Check species identity.','Check changing species.','Check role attached to reactant evidence.'],['remove role labels','include spectator information'],'same role logic in a new equation',['Agent vocabulary beyond recorded source/capability scope is not introduced.']),
      A('PCK-CHEM-STRUCTURE-SITE','STRUCTURE_SITE_REASONING',['CAP-READ-STRUCTURE-SITE'],'Make the specific structural site visible before any whole-formula shortcut.',['Annotate distinct sites.','Bind the property/rule to the site rather than an average alone.'],'When sites are non-equivalent, a whole-formula average can hide the distinction the question needs.','Requires an authorized structural representation.',['Locate sites.','Mark non-equivalence.','Apply the site-specific rule.','Recombine/check the whole species.'],'Use a source-authorized structural contrast where the decisive site changes.','PF-STRUCTURE_SITE_REASONING','One average value necessarily describes every site.','Ask which atom/site the question is actually referring to.',['Return to the structure.','Label sites individually.','Retry site-by-site.'],['Check site identity.','Check the structural dependency.'],['remove site labels','require learner annotation'],'new structure with the same site-sensitive mechanism',['Inactive when structure/site reasoning is outside declared scope.'],app=['Use only when declared/source scope explicitly requires structure- or site-sensitive reasoning.']),
      A('PCK-CHEM-PRACTICAL-METHOD','PRACTICAL_METHOD_PROPERTY_LINK',['CAP-READ-APPARATUS-METHOD'],'Start from the property/evidence needed, then connect it to the apparatus or method feature.',['Target property → apparatus feature → expected observation/use.'],'Choose the method because of the property it exploits, not because the diagram looks familiar.','Only apparatus/method properties authorized by source may be used.',['Identify target property.','Identify apparatus feature.','Link feature to property.','Verify against the goal/observation.'],'Compare two visually similar method representations that differ on the decisive property link.','PF-PRACTICAL_METHOD_SELECTION','Recognizing the apparatus shape is enough.','Ask what property makes this method or apparatus suitable.',['Name the property first.','Trace it to the apparatus feature.','Retry with labels removed.'],['Check property-method link.','Check the target observation/goal.'],['remove labels','change diagram orientation'],'same property-method link in a different representation',['Does not introduce laboratory procedures or safety claims absent from scope.']),
      A('PCK-CHEM-VERIFICATION','CHEMICAL_VERIFICATION',['CAP-VERIFY-CHEMICAL-REPRESENTATION','CAP-CHECK-ATOM-CONSERVATION','CAP-PARSE-ION-CHARGE'],'Make checking a separate pass, not a repetition of the final answer.',['Run only applicable checks: species identity, atoms, charge, units, state/condition and plausibility.'],'A tidy final answer is not chemically verified until an independent check is applied.','Verification obligations are inherited from source/problem-family authority.',['Name the required checks.','Run each independently.','Locate any failure.','Repair.','Re-run.'],'Contrast a neat-looking result with one that passes the required chemical invariant.','PF-CHEMICAL_VERIFICATION','Getting an answer means it has been checked.','Ask which independent chemical check could still make the result fail.',['Choose one independent check.','Apply it.','Repair and repeat.'],['Check route-specific invariants.'],['remove checklist labels','require learner-selected check'],'verification on a new representation/problem family',['Do not force checks that are not semantically applicable.']),
      A('PCK-CHEM-MINIMAL-CONTRAST','MISCONCEPTION_MINIMAL_CONTRAST',['CAP-READ-FORMULA','CAP-PARSE-ION-CHARGE','CAP-CHECK-RULE-EXCEPTION','CAP-SEPARATE-OBSERVATION-INFERENCE','CAP-ATTACH-SPECIES-ROLE'],'Show the smallest pair that makes a plausible wrong model fail.',['Hold irrelevant features constant.','Change one decisive notation, condition, evidence or role feature.'],'A warning is not a repair; the learner must see why the wrong model fails and retry.','Use only contrasts whose decisive feature is authorized by the active scope.',['State the plausible wrong model.','Predict both cases.','Expose the decisive difference.','Repair the model.','Retry.'],'A minimal pair differing on exactly one decisive feature.','PF-MINIMAL_CHEMISTRY_CONTRAST','A bold warning or mnemonic repairs the underlying model.','Ask for a prediction on a close contrast before explaining.',['Elicit the wrong model.','Show the discriminating contrast.','State the repaired model.','Retry immediately.'],['Check learner prediction.','Check repaired explanation.'],['remove explanation labels','increase surface similarity'],'same discriminator in a new surface context',['Use only when the wrong model is relevant to the active capability.']),
      A('PCK-CHEM-FIRST-MOVE','FIRST_MOVE_DECISION_SUPPORT',['CAP-READ-FORMULA','CAP-PARSE-ION-CHARGE','CAP-TRANSLATE-PARTICLE-SYMBOL','CAP-CHECK-ATOM-CONSERVATION','CAP-CHECK-RULE-EXCEPTION','CAP-CLASSIFY-CHANGE-EVIDENCE','CAP-PRESERVE-REACTION-CONDITION','CAP-SEPARATE-OBSERVATION-INFERENCE','CAP-READ-APPARATUS-METHOD','CAP-TRACK-REACTING-SPECIES','CAP-ATTACH-SPECIES-ROLE','CAP-VERIFY-CHEMICAL-REPRESENTATION'],'Reduce search by making the first chemically meaningful decision explicit.',['Question cue → first representation/action → check.'],'A first move should expose the governing evidence, representation or rule without giving away the result.','Decision support cannot add chemistry beyond the active StudyModel.',['Identify the target.','Choose the first move.','Expose the needed evidence.','Continue independently.'],'Use two similar-looking prompts requiring different justified first moves.','PF-FIRST_MOVE_DECISION_SUPPORT','A keyword automatically selects the method.','Ask what information is still needed if the keyword is removed.',['Restate the target.','Select representation/evidence.','Retry without the cue.'],['Check the first move is justified by givens.'],['fade the cue','replace cue with learner-generated first move'],'first-move selection in mixed practice',['Cannot substitute for full teaching in ACTIVE_STUDY or REPAIR.']),
      A('PCK-REDOX-OXIDATION-LANE','REDOX_OXIDATION_STATE_LANES',['CAP-TRACK-OXIDATION-STATE'],'Track the same element/species from before to after on an oxidation-state lane.',['Write before and after oxidation states.','Mark increase/decrease before naming the process.'],'Direction of oxidation-state change is evidence; reagent reputation is not.','Topic-scoped Redox asset.',['Assign source-authorized oxidation states.','Link the same entity.','Compare values.','Classify direction.'],'Opposite oxidation-state directions on the same visual axis.','PF-OXIDATION_STATE_TRACKING','Oxidation/reduction can be named from a familiar reagent.','Ask which numerical direction is actually shown.',['Rebuild the lane.','State increase/decrease.','Retry without mnemonic.'],['Check oxidation-state assignment.','Check same entity is tracked.'],['remove direction labels','use a multi-species equation'],'oxidation-state direction in a new Redox equation',['Inactive outside declared Redox scope.'],topics=['REDOX'],app=['TOPIC_SCOPE=REDOX and oxidation-state tracking is explicitly required.']),
